WEBVTT

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>The year is 2205 A.D.</i>

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:14.020
<i>To annihilate the History Retrograde 
Army, who scheme to alter history,</i>

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.150
<i>we, who were born from swords,</i>

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.760
<i>engage in mortal combat today as well!</i>

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.660
<i>Dance with this little fox.</i>

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:43.370
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:59.410
"This anime is about the 
stories of the Hanamaru days

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:04.210
of a certain group of Sword 
Warriors in a certain citadel."

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.590
This is for me?

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.310
Thanks.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:13.080
Let's see...

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.380
Eh, what's that?

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.590
Well, I think that's appropriate.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:23.660
45 - Ootachi 
<b>Hotarumaru</b>

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.660
Right. If I think of anything, I'll
ask Hotarumaru and the others.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:25.370
46 - Tachi 
<b>Akashi Kuniyuki</b>

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.720
Man, what a talkative person.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:33.520
Now then, what time is dinner?

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.970
No one saw us, right?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:39.640
Yeah.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:45.050
What's this? Looking at your guardian 
with such scary expressions...

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:47.310
Hey, Kuniyuki.

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:51.420
We're going to go greet
everyone in the citadel now,

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:53.730
so could you act a bit more proper, please.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.580
"A bit more proper"?

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:57.760
You mean me?

00:02:57.890 --> 00:02:58.850
Yes.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.860
Well, none of that particularly suits me.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.650
First impressions are important!

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.860
Be friendly and proper, please.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.440
Aren't I?

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.230
I'm proper.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:15.400
The "Friendly Strategy"
might be a bit difficult.

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:20.660
What? Getting all secretive 
all of a sudden? What's up?

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.150
We've been talking about how we might 
get you more used to being here.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:28.380
Gosh, you're really worried 
about that, aren't you?

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:30.510
Well, you hate working, don't you?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.640
Having no motivation is my specialty.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.980
That's what we're worried about!

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.760
Caring is kind of an important 
part of living here.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.270
Right, Hotarumaru?

00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:42.890
Yeah.

00:03:42.890 --> 00:03:45.950
Try not to expect anything from me.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:52.640
Don't look at me like that. I can't just 
suddenly care because you tell me to.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.500
There's lot's of things, like—

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.280
Helping people when they're in trouble.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:57.920
That's right!

00:03:58.340 --> 00:04:01.420
And more of us means more housework.

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:03.150
Like weeding!

00:04:03.150 --> 00:04:04.210
Cleaning!

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:07.110
Folding laundry and washing dishes.

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.690
My specialty is eating, though.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:13.050
I want you to like it here,

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:15.200
and I want everyone here to like you.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:16.750
Kuniyuki?

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:19.650
Bathroom.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.990
Ah, I'll take you to it.

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.940
It's just down the hall, right?

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.740
I know where it is, we passed it earlier.

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.360
But...

00:04:32.030 --> 00:04:34.090
We probably said too much.

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:35.610
He did only just get here.

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.160
But if we didn't go that 
far, he wouldn't get it.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.500
You're right, but...

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.330
You're worried.

00:04:42.530 --> 00:04:43.560
I get it.

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:45.800
Knowing Kuniyuki,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:51.470
he'd start out saying stuff like,
"There's no need to greet one another."

00:04:57.630 --> 00:05:01.360
Well, we probably did go 
a bit too far, though.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.220
He's taking a while.

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.340
Yeah...

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.690
You think he knows the way back?

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:17.620
What is it?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.820
I just took my eyes off it for 
a moment and the crops...

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:22.800
They're all destroyed!

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.960
They were just about ready to be harvested!

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.920
This is awful.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.710
Ah, what an atrocity.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:30.290
What could have done this?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:32.120
Some kind of beast?

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:34.430
The number of traps may not be enough.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.550
Aren't these shoe prints?

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.370
What is it?

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.870
We were getting ready to 
roast some sweet potatoes.

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:54.630
Wh-When we came back from getting the 
potatoes, all the fallen leaves were gone.

00:05:55.340 --> 00:05:58.170
Maybe someone thought they were 
trash and threw them away?

00:05:58.330 --> 00:06:00.170
I guess I'll rake some up again.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.240
Wh-What is this?!

00:06:04.450 --> 00:06:09.430
They were white and elegantly blowing 
in the autumn wind until just now.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:12.940
Now they're all filthy and messed up.

00:06:12.940 --> 00:06:14.010
Filthy?

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:15.620
The bedding.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:16.730
Look at this.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:21.420
Rather than falling from the clothes line, 
they've all been taken down and neatly folded.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.080
Who in the world could have done this?

00:06:24.390 --> 00:06:26.370
There's no way, is there?

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:29.940
It can't be. Kuniyuki wouldn't do that.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:32.570
Eating is his specialty, after all.

00:06:32.570 --> 00:06:34.120
What is it, you two?

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.280
Do you know something?

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:35.670
No!

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:35.670
Nope!

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:37.900
Could it be an intruder?

00:06:37.900 --> 00:06:40.160
That would mean the History—

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.030
Retrograde Army?!

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.510
You don't think Kuniyuki could
 have done this, do you?

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.560
Do you think Kuniyuki's a likely culprit?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.340
Either way, we need to find him, and fast.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:52.930
Yeah.

00:06:57.640 --> 00:06:58.610
Huh?

00:06:58.870 --> 00:07:00.830
Where are the rice balls I just made?

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.920
The plate disappeared, too?

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:05.220
What's going on?

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.230
I wonder if that jerk Kuniyuki was hungry.

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:11.660
Eating is his specialty, after all.

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:15.750
Kuniyuki!

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.750
Oh, how scary. Why are you two so pale?

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:22.260
Was it you, Kuniyuki?

00:07:22.860 --> 00:07:26.540
Let's go. We'll apologize with 
you, if you've got an excuse.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.690
What are you talking about?

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:32.100
You were the one behind everything, right?

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.090
What's the meaning of this?

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:36.590
I haven't seen you around here before.

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:38.310
Are you a newcomer?

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:41.220
I'm Akashi Kuniyuki.

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.760
Nice to meet you.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:44.350
What's that?

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.570
Ah, I was hungry.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.880
You're the one who dirtied the bedding?

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:51.670
My hand slipped.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.590
And the one who damaged the crops?

00:07:53.730 --> 00:07:54.360
Yes.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.400
And threw away the fallen leaves.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:57.820
It was all me.

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.530
He's quite the mischievous type.

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:01.580
No!

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.680
He's not!

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:07.130
Kuniyuki was only doing what we told him 
to do, but he just got a bit carried away!

00:08:07.240 --> 00:08:08.830
You don't have to lie.

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:10.050
But—

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:14.700
Who was it that took some 
medicine from my room?

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:15.170
Huh?

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:16.880
You did that, too?

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:18.450
It was me.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.350
Why would you do that?

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:23.190
What is that?

00:08:23.370 --> 00:08:24.120
Eh?

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.110
You shouldn't come out.

00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.060
It can't be.

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:37.820
This is...

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:39.780
Then are these leaves...

00:08:40.050 --> 00:08:41.210
Kuniyuki?

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:44.270
This has become rather troublesome.

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:45.760
What's going on?

00:08:46.850 --> 00:08:49.690
I heard them when I was coming 
back from the bathroom.

00:08:52.180 --> 00:08:54.420
These guys were wailing.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:59.400
I wondered where the mother went since
she left her pups behind, so I went looking.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:01.780
Good grief...

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:14.220
Well, she's a pretty careless tanuki.

00:09:15.870 --> 00:09:19.870
Then, the ones who caused all 
that mischief were the tanuki?

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:23.920
No, I was the one doing all the borrowing.

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.620
But all that was for the tanuki, right?

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:28.510
Well, yeah.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:30.080
How kind of you.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:32.500
Man, you had us worried.

00:09:32.810 --> 00:09:34.590
All this sure isn't like you.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:38.920
Well, it's because I know 
how a guardian feels.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:43.860
Besides, caring is an important 
part of living here, right?

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:48.280
All's well that ends well.

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:50.670
I'll just rewash the laundry.

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:55.440
Okay, we'll start prepping for 
Akashi-kun's welcome party.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:57.600
Ah, I'll help you.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:00.780
You don't have to do that for me.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:02.690
Don't give it a second thought.

00:10:02.690 --> 00:10:05.280
It's not every day a new comrade joins us.

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:06.750
That's right!

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:08.560
Hey, let me look me take a look at her.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:10.270
I'll treat her wound.

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:11.450
Thank you.

00:10:12.320 --> 00:10:14.740
He's going to fit in pretty well.

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:17.690
There was no reason for us to worry.

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.010
Nope.

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:22.830
Hotarumaru, Aizen Kunitoshi,

00:10:23.020 --> 00:10:25.710
I need you to show me around after all.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:27.820
Sure!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:27.820
Okay!

00:10:28.770 --> 00:10:31.020
<b>Touken Ranbu </b>Hanamaru<b></b>

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.240
Whoa, it looks so good!

00:10:35.290 --> 00:10:36.460
Hot!

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:38.780
That's why I said to be careful.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:45.570
Red bean paste definitely goes
 with roasted sweet potato!

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.410
So good!

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:51.750
Jeez! It's flying everywhere, though.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:53.320
Now, now.

00:10:53.650 --> 00:10:56.710
Doesn't this mayonnaise stuff 
go with anything, though?

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:00.100
Yuck!

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:01.750
What is this?

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.060
This won't do!

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:04.840
Come on, Kuniyuki, that's gross.

00:11:05.450 --> 00:11:07.590
You should try it, too, Hotarumaru.

00:11:07.670 --> 00:11:08.650
Here.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.350
I don't want it.

00:11:12.110 --> 00:11:14.260
A fun person has joined us.

00:11:14.260 --> 00:11:16.360
Yes, so it would seem.

00:11:16.850 --> 00:11:20.150
Akashi-san is the 46th Sword Warrior.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:23.440
It becomes more lively with each day.

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:31.800
Iwatooshi!

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:33.420
Aren't they hot?

00:11:35.260 --> 00:11:38.340
As expected of Musashibou Benkei's naginata.

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.220
He's just as lively.

00:11:41.510 --> 00:11:42.990
Mikazuki-sama!

00:11:42.990 --> 00:11:46.390
Does that mean I'm handsome, 
like Lord Yoshitsune?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:49.760
It might.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:52.020
Yay!

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:59.190
You're also probably similar to the 
Shinsengumi's Okita Souji, Yamatonokami-san!

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:02.860
"Probably."

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:05.600
Jeez.

00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:12.500
Yamatonokami is also skilled 
with a blade, like Okita Souji.

00:12:12.760 --> 00:12:15.950
He's been through a number of deadly battles.

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:20.640
Yamatonokami-san and Kashuu-san 
are vital to this citadel.

00:12:21.730 --> 00:12:24.020
So he says. I'm glad.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:25.930
Me, too.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:30.910
What's the matter?

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:32.760
Nothing.

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:37.350
I was just wondering what kind of person 
Kogitsunemaru-san's former master was.

00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:38.640
Oh?

00:12:39.370 --> 00:12:40.830
How long have you been there?

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.600
Honebami Toushirou.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.140
You're the attendant at the moment, right?

00:12:46.140 --> 00:12:47.550
Did you need something?

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:49.320
Dispatch orders.

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:49.950
<b>Sa</b>

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:56.460
Yamatonokami Yasusada, Mikazuki 
Munechika, and Kogitsunemaru.

00:12:56.690 --> 00:12:58.450
I will gladly serve.

00:12:58.450 --> 00:13:01.450
Indeed. Shall we go, then?

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:09.180
Also, Yagen Toushirou, Tsurumaru Kuninaga, 
and the captain is Ichigo Hitofuri.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.920
I'll go tell Yagen and the others.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:13.400
Please get ready.

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:23.480
An uchigatana, tantou, and four tachi.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:28.330
We have an interesting unit formation 
today, Captain Ichigo Hitofuri.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:32.260
Master seems to be trying 
out different combinations.

00:13:32.520 --> 00:13:34.990
Ichi-nii, please take care of me.

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:40.400
I'm happy to be going into battle 
with one of the Five Great Swords.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:44.930
I'll be glad if this old man can be useful.

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.330
Festival music?

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:51.550
Eh? I can't hear anything.

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:53.300
You have good hearing.

00:13:53.300 --> 00:13:54.910
Because I'm a wild animal.

00:13:57.930 --> 00:13:59.050
Gunfire?

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:05.560
Surprises are necessary 
in both life and battle.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:06.850
The enemy knows that, too.

00:14:07.460 --> 00:14:08.800
We let our guard down.

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:11.020
Get ready, everyone.

00:14:11.390 --> 00:14:12.660
Kogitsunemaru?

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.260
I'm fine.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.370
However, the comb Master gave me...

00:14:23.920 --> 00:14:26.420
Now it's our turn to surprise them!

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:30.680
Now then... I guess it's time 
we work for our wages.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:31.550
Now,

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:34.890
going forth.

00:14:35.710 --> 00:14:37.980
There you are. Time to strike!

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:50.370
Tsurumaru, can I leave this to you?

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.640
Where are you going?

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.380
Kogitsunemaru.

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:57.090
Since he only recently arrived, he does
 not have much battle experience.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:59.740
Leave this to us.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:41.960
I'll run you through to the hilt.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.080
Kogitsunemaru!

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:51.890
Let's help them.

00:15:51.890 --> 00:15:52.580
Right.

00:15:53.980 --> 00:15:57.270
I didn't think I'd have to get serious.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:09.350
S-So cool.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:11.410
Well done.

00:16:12.100 --> 00:16:13.520
Is that all of them?

00:16:13.710 --> 00:16:15.020
There was one more.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:17.960
Ichigo Hitofuri and Yagen went after it.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:32.980
Rain?

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:35.800
The sky is clear, though.

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.640
I wonder if they're all right.

00:16:38.920 --> 00:16:40.770
There's only one enemy left.

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.000
I don't think there's any cause 
for concern with those two.

00:16:57.380 --> 00:16:58.500
That's...

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:05.480
Kogitsunemaru-san,

00:17:06.230 --> 00:17:07.520
are you all right?

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:10.000
Your wounds must hurt.

00:17:10.330 --> 00:17:12.510
Ah, I'm fine.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:15.160
Oh, what good luck.

00:17:15.160 --> 00:17:17.590
Shall we wait out the rain in that hut?

00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.680
Excuse us.

00:17:31.570 --> 00:17:34.400
So this is a blacksmith's hut?

00:17:34.400 --> 00:17:36.480
There's still a fire going.

00:17:36.630 --> 00:17:38.400
There must still be someone here.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:42.480
Who said you could enter, kon?

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.840
The crane turned into a fox, did he?

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:50.990
Jeez, you're just helping yourself. 
What if they come back?

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:54.070
I'm sure it's fine!

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:56.460
Besides, you'll catch 
a cold if you're soaked.

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:58.710
Now, let's all get changed.

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:15.400
Here you are.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:19.030
I'm really glad there was a hut here.

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:23.750
After we've rested a bit, let's go 
find Ichigo Hitofuri and Yagen.

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:26.950
When Munechika strikes with his hammer...

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:29.980
...the fox god becomes a halberd.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:32.800
What's that?

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.090
"Kokaji."

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.600
It's Kogitsunemaru's song.

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:40.030
Oh, Kogitsunemaru's?

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.320
What kind of song is it?

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:42.800
Please, tell me more about it.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:49.330
Tachibana Michinari, upon receiving 
orders from Emperor Ichijou,

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:54.600
ordered the famous swordsmith, 
Sanjou Munechika, to forge a sword.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:59.820
However, that sword was not something 
Munechika could craft on his own.

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:05.290
The troubled Munechika sought 
help from the great god Inari.

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:09.680
Upon hearing the pleas of Sanjou Munechika,

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:14.850
the great god took the form of a fox 
spirit and appeared before him.

00:19:15.370 --> 00:19:17.920
It is said that by working together,

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:21.500
the two were able to create a splendid sword.

00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:30.110
And that sword is Kogitsunemaru.

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:36.650
Throughout the ages, many people have 
passed along this beloved song.

00:19:37.430 --> 00:19:41.750
"Kokaji" is the song about
how Kogitsunemaru was forged.

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:45.870
Kogitsunemaru's dignified 
appearance and sword strength

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:50.940
might be from all of the feelings he
has received from people beyond that period.

00:19:51.130 --> 00:19:52.900
Probably, kon.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:55.930
You're going to joke around there?

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:57.120
Kon, kon.

00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:01.260
That's enough with the little 
fox stories, isn't it?

00:20:08.620 --> 00:20:09.880
Oh?

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:15.260
I wonder what it feels like.

00:20:17.000 --> 00:20:20.950
To have your song passed 
down through the ages.

00:20:20.950 --> 00:20:25.380
I have no idea, but I guess 
I would feel pretty proud.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:27.460
And you, Tsurumaru-san?

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:30.570
Well, if that happened...

00:20:30.570 --> 00:20:31.780
You'd be surprised?

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:36.430
Everyone?

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.740
Huh... this is?

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:42.470
What are you doing?

00:20:42.690 --> 00:20:45.200
Oh my, the sake...

00:20:46.430 --> 00:20:47.630
This is a surprise.

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:49.800
We're the ones who are surprised.

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:52.600
What were you doing out here in the grass?

00:20:52.870 --> 00:20:56.190
Well, um... Uh... huh?

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.610
We've been tricked by the foxes, huh?

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:00.720
My wounds are healed.

00:21:02.680 --> 00:21:03.650
My comb was fixed, too.

00:21:03.820 --> 00:21:05.750
Eh, how?

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.420
What a conscientious fellow.

00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:18.330
How interesting.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:21.790
What do you mean? Please, explain.

00:21:21.940 --> 00:21:24.420
How do I report this to Master?

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:26.890
Now, now, we'll explain it to you later.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.800
This will also be a wonderful memory.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:31.350
You're right.

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:35.350
<i>It is because of a song that I am here.</i>

00:21:36.030 --> 00:21:40.470
<i>I will make the time I spend with everyone 
at the citadel into precious memories.</i>

00:21:40.470 --> 00:21:42.000
<i>And keep them here.</i>

00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.460
<i>I also have precious memories,</i>

00:21:45.630 --> 00:21:48.110
<i>of Okita-kun and the Shinsengumi.</i>

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.320
<i>It's okay to remember, isn't it?</i>

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:52.950
<i>Just for today.</i>

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:28.420
<b>Sa</b>

00:23:33.260 --> 00:23:40.350
47 - Uchigatana
 <b>Nagasone Kotetsu</b>

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:35.340
I am Nagasone Kotetsu,

00:23:35.340 --> 00:23:39.600
beloved sword of Kondou Isami, 
commander of the Shinsengumi.

00:23:41.180 --> 00:23:42.940
Nagasone Kotetsu.

00:23:43.580 --> 00:23:47.190
I may be a fake, but I will work 
harder than a real Kotetsu.

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:48.600
It's you.

00:23:48.600 --> 00:23:50.040
Yamatonokami Yasusada, huh?

00:23:50.500 --> 00:23:53.980
Nagasone-san, you've finally arrived.

00:23:55.030 --> 00:24:00.030
<b>More Hanamaru Next Week!</b>
